%erg v1
Title: Fix erg check false positives — archive/ dir and module name mismatch
Created: 2026-05-06
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-06T00:00Z claude created — two false positives in erg check surfaced during housekeeping

--- body ---
## Problem

`erg check` emits spurious warnings in this repo:

1. **strayGoSource module name mismatch**: `strayGoSource()` in `check.go`
   suppresses the warning when `go.mod` contains
   `module github.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg`, but the actual module name is
   `module git-erg`. The string match fails, so the warning fires in the
   development repo itself — a self-referential false positive.

## Fix

1. Fix `strayGoSource()` to also accept `module git-erg` (or use a
   less fragile check, e.g. split on whitespace and match the module name
   without the host prefix).

## Acceptance

- `erg check tickets/` in this repo emits 0 warnings (after fix).
- Existing tests pass; add regression cases for both checks.
- Binary rebuilt: `make build` succeeds, `make test` green.
